        \subsubsection{Python Threads results}
        Similarly to its C++ counterpart, the Python implementation was evaluated across 15 test runs using the same input datasets (\textit{rockyou.txt} to populate the dictionary and \textit{parole\_uniche.txt} to measure the false positive rate). The results are summarized below:
        
        \begin{table}[H]
            \centering
            \caption{Performance results per cycle}
            \label{tab:performance_cycle_python}
            \resizebox{\textwidth}{!}{%
            \begin{tabular}{c cccc cccc c}
                \toprule
                & \multicolumn{4}{c}{\textbf{ADD}} & \multicolumn{4}{c}{\textbf{CONTAINS}} & \\
                \cmidrule(lr){2-5} \cmidrule(lr){6-9}
